<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
    <%- include('partials/google-tag') %>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Startup idea review | Arrington Consultancy</title>
    <%# HIDDEN LANDING PAGE (Tom, 06/10/2026). noindex here and as an
        X-Robots-Tag header from the route. Not in the sitemap, not in the
        navigation, not linked from anywhere else. See routes/startUpReview.js. %>
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <meta name="description" content="Have your startup idea looked at before you put your money in. A fixed £500 setup review from someone who has built, grown and sold his own business. The first conversation is free.">
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/start-up-idea-review">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:title" content="Startup idea review | Arrington Consultancy">
    <meta property="og:description" content="Before you put your money into a startup, have the idea looked at by someone who has built, grown and sold real businesses.">
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/start-up-idea-review">
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/img/logo">
    <meta name="csrf-token" content="<%= csrfToken %>">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <%# No Product/Offer schema, deliberately: the page is noindex and the
        offer's deliverables are not yet confirmed. %>
    <style nonce="<%= nonce %>">
        :root {
            <% for (const [prop, val] of Object.entries(theme.vars)) { %>
            <%= prop %>: <%= val %>;
            <% } %>
        }
        * { box-sizing: border-box; }
        body { margin: 0; font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; background: var(--black); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.6; }
        <%- include('partials/site-chrome-styles') %>

        h1, h2, h3 { font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; font-weight: 500; color: var(--text-bright); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0; }
        p { color: var(--text); margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }

        .btn { display: inline-block; font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 600; padding: 0.6rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 3px; text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid transparent; }
        .btn-primary { background: var(--accent); color: var(--black); border-color: var(--accent); }
        .btn-primary:hover, .btn-primary:focus-visible { background: var(--accent-hover); border-color: var(--accent-hover); }

        main { max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; padding: calc(var(--site-chrome) + 2.5rem) 1.5rem 5rem; }

        /* The same page grammar as the sale readiness landing page
           (views/sale-readiness.ejs), which Tom reviewed live on 25/09/2026:
           label, headline, lede, a single primary button, then a de-boxed
           credibility line with hairline rules. Nothing new is invented here. */
        .su-label { font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 1rem; display: block; }
        h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.5vw, 2.4rem); margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
        .su-lede { font-size: 1.12rem; color: var(--text-bright); margin-bottom: 1.6rem; max-width: 62ch; }
        .su-hero-actions { margin-bottom: 0; }

        .su-cred {
            margin-top: 2.5rem;
            padding: 1.5rem 0;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        }
        .su-cred p { margin: 0; font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--text-bright); }
        .su-cred p + p { margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.97rem; }

        .su-section { margin-top: 3.25rem; }
        .su-section > h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
        .su-section > .su-intro { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 1.6rem; max-width: 62ch; }

        .su-card { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.9rem 2rem; }
        .su-card > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

        .su-price-row {
            display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.9rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
            margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        }
        .su-price-fig { font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; font-weight: 500; font-size: 1.9rem; color: var(--accent); line-height: 1; }
        .su-price-row p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.94rem; color: var(--text-muted); }

        /* Accent-dot list, the site's existing list treatment (Owner Check,
           sale readiness) rather than the browser's default discs. */
        .su-dots { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; max-width: 62ch; }
        .su-dots li { position: relative; padding-left: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; font-size: 0.98rem; color: var(--text); }
        .su-dots li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
        .su-dots strong { color: var(--text-bright); font-weight: 700; }
        .su-includes { max-width: none; }
        .su-dots li::before {
            content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.6em;
            width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent);
        }

        .su-section.su-who > h2 { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }

        .su-final { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 2.5rem; margin-top: 3.5rem; }
        .su-final h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
        .su-final p { max-width: 62ch; }
        .su-final-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.9rem; margin-top: 1.6rem; }
        .su-aside { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 1.6rem; }
        .su-aside a {
            color: var(--accent);
            text-decoration: none;
            border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent);
            padding-bottom: 2px;
        }
        .su-aside a:hover, .su-aside a:focus-visible { border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }
        .su-next { max-width: 62ch; margin-top: 1.1rem; }
        .su-get-lead { color: var(--text-bright); margin: 1.6rem 0 0; max-width: 62ch; }
        .su-website > p { max-width: 62ch; }
        .su-website > h2 + p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
        .su-price-fig-minor { font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-bright); }

        @media (max-width: 760px) {
            main { padding-top: calc(var(--site-chrome) + 1.75rem); }
            .su-section { margin-top: 2.1rem; }
            .su-section > h2 { margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
            .su-section > .su-intro { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
            .su-cred { margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1.25rem 0; }
            .su-card { padding: 1.4rem 1.25rem; }
            .su-final { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.9rem; }
            .su-hero-actions .btn, .su-final-actions .btn { width: 100%; text-align: center; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <%# currentPage carries a slug that is deliberately not in navPages: this
        is a hidden campaign landing page (Tom, 06/10/2026), so nothing in the
        nav highlights as active. Header and footer are the site's own. %>
    <%- include('partials/site-header', { currentPage: { slug: 'start-up-idea-review' }, navPages, canEdit: false, content, pageContact }) %>

    <main>
        <%# HERO. The headline is Tom's own (06/10/2026). Rewritten the same
            day in Tom's voice (Professional Tom Voice Programme and Arrington
            Voice rules in Drive): fewer, fuller paragraphs, a hook that names
            the mistakes a new owner is about to make, no dashes, and nothing
            under the headline that repeats it. Facts are only the approved
            ones: built, grew and sold his own business in a seven figure exit,
            more than 20 years in Devon and Cornwall businesses, £500 and £999. %>
        <span class="su-label">Startup idea review</span>
        <h1>Before you put your money into a startup, have the idea looked at with fresh eyes with 20 years' experience of building and scaling businesses.</h1>
        <p class="su-lede">The expensive mistakes in a new business usually happen early. A name you have to change six months in, a company structure that doesn't suit how you'll actually pay yourself, a bank account set up the wrong way, or marketing money spent before you know who your customers are. We go through all of it with you before you commit, for a fixed £500, and the first conversation costs you nothing.</p>
        <div class="su-hero-actions">
            <a href="#conversation" class="btn btn-primary">Tell us about the idea</a>
        </div>

        <div class="su-cred">
            <p>Oxford Saïd, Distinction. 5.0 on Google reviews.</p>
            <p>The owner run businesses we usually work with have been trading for years. This is for the step before that.</p>
        </div>

        <%# HOW IT WORKS: one paragraph rather than a numbered card. The
            "about 30 minutes (always more)" aside is Tom's own, approved in
            the voice programme on 05/10/2026. %>
        <div class="su-section">
            <h2>How it works</h2>
            <p>Tell us about the idea using the form at the bottom of the page. A few lines is plenty: what the business would do, who you think will pay for it and how far you've got. We'll then sit down with you for about 30 minutes (always more) and ask the questions we'd ask before putting our own money in, so you come away knowing where the idea really stands. If the review is the right next step, we go through the idea and the setup with you properly, for a fixed £500.</p>
        </div>

        <%# WHAT THE £500 REVIEW COVERS. The five items are Tom's, given on
            06/10/2026, in his order. A list because they are genuinely five
            separate things. Arrington gives no regulated financial or
            accountancy advice, so items three and four say what to sort out
            with a bank and with an accountant. %>
        <div class="su-section">
            <h2>What the £500 setup review covers</h2>
            <div class="su-price-row">
                <span class="su-price-fig">£500</span>
                <p>Fixed and agreed before any work starts.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="su-card">
                <ul class="su-dots su-includes" data-deliverables="5">
                    <li><strong>Brand guidance.</strong> Your name, your look and how you describe what you do, settled before you pay to put them on anything.</li>
                    <li><strong>Company structure advice.</strong> Sole trader, partnership or limited company, and which one actually suits the way you plan to run the business and pay yourself.</li>
                    <li><strong>What to sort out with a bank.</strong> Getting set up to take payments and pay out cleanly from your very first sale.</li>
                    <li><strong>What to sort out with an accountant.</strong> The records worth keeping from day one, and when it's worth bringing an accountant in.</li>
                    <li><strong>Marketing advice.</strong> Where your first customers are most likely to come from, and what's actually worth spending to reach them.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="su-get-lead"><strong>We treat your money as if it's our own.</strong> You get a straight view of the idea from someone who has built, grown and sold a business, clear answers on all five areas worked out for your idea, and a clear next step at the end of it.</p>
        </div>

        <%# THE WEBSITE BUILD, BELOW THE REVIEW (Tom, 06/10/2026). Tom's words:
            "HTML site a completely customisable non templated sites". £999 is
            the approved public Website Build price (lib/whereToStartOffers.js),
            never framed as a reduction or an offer that ends. Visually smaller
            than the review: muted figure, no button. Links go OUT only. %>
        <div class="su-section su-website">
            <h2>A website for your startup</h2>
            <p>Once the idea is sound, we can build the website too: an HTML site built from scratch, not from a template, and completely customisable. You'll have a recorded planning conversation to agree what it needs to do, a complete first version and one structured round of changes before launch.</p>
            <div class="su-price-row">
                <span class="su-price-fig su-price-fig-minor">£999</span>
                <p>Fixed.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="su-aside su-next">See the <a href="/where-to-start/website-build">Website Build</a>, or how we approach <a href="/websites-and-ai">websites and AI</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <%# WHO YOU WOULD BE TALKING TO. Third person for Tom's story, per the
            Brand OS. Proof is the approved operator proof only. %>
        <div class="su-section su-who">
            <h2>Who you'd be talking to</h2>
            <p>Tom Arrington built, grew and sold his own business in a seven figure exit, and has spent more than 20 years inside real businesses across Devon and Cornwall. He's been where you are, with his own money on the line, which is why the review starts with the questions he'd want answered himself.</p>
        </div>

        <%# FINAL CALL TO ACTION: the existing footer enquiry form
            (#conversation), the only form that fires the Contact conversion.
            No checkout on this page. %>
        <div class="su-final">
            <h2>Tell us about the idea</h2>
            <p>A few lines is plenty to start. We'll come back to you to arrange a conversation, and you'll get a straight answer on whether the review is worth your money.</p>
            <div class="su-final-actions">
                <a href="#conversation" class="btn btn-primary">Tell us about the idea</a>
            </div>
            <p class="su-aside">Rather talk? The phone number and WhatsApp are at the bottom of the page.</p>
        </div>
    </main>

    <%- include('partials/site-footer', { canEdit: false, pageContact, content }) %>
    <script nonce="<%= nonce %>">
        <%- include('partials/site-chrome-script') %>
    </script>
</body>
</html>
